35,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
37,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
38,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
39,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
40,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My findings remind us that we must be careful with things we cannot control. I noticed that our scanning contractors' delivery dates can slip if larger clients come first, which could be quite stressful for us.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My research reveals a quiet struggle with accessibility. Residents in the outer wards have lost their bus links, and our remote catalogue use peaks long after our doors are locked for the evening.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found some super cool secrets! A long time ago, we tried some things that actually worked really well, like outreach stops that way more people visited than the main library! But some other things just got left unfinished.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are all uncovering a symphony of systemic frictions. My review suggests a precarious financial dance: our grants provide a temporary flourish of funding that vanishes after a year, leaving the flat budget to shoulder the burden.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings indicate a critical gap in our operational capacity. While we have skilled volunteers, we lack any staff on the payroll trained to supervise outside facilitators, and we no longer have a certified technician for power tools.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, that sounds like a heavy burden for our volunteers. It would be so sad if they felt overwhelmed. We must find a path that is gentle on our people and doesn't rely on things that might slip away.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I agree. It is also concerning that our physical boundaries are becoming barriers. If people in the outer wards cannot reach us and our hours are too restrictive, we are unintentionally excluding those who seek knowledge.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, that's exactly why the outreach stops were so great! People loved them because the library came to them! We shouldn't just talk about new ideas; we should look at what already worked!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, your enthusiasm for the past is noted, but we must be wary of nostalgia. A project that flourished once may now be a financial liability if the funding structure has shifted from a temporary grant to a stagnant operating budget.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, you are correct that funding is a risk, but the human risk is equally tangible. If we implement a project requiring specialized supervision or tool certification, we are simply adding a commitment to a roster that cannot support it.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, you are so right to worry about the staff. It would be a shame to start something wonderful only to have it fall apart because we were too optimistic. We should seek a plan that is steady and reliable.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Rin, the success of those outreach stops is a hopeful sign. If we can bridge the gap for those in the outer wards without adding undue stress to our staff, we might find a truly harmonious solution.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, yes! That's what I mean! And @Benjamin, it's not just nostalgia—it's like a map! If we ignore the map, we might walk right into a hole that someone else already fell into six years ago!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, a map is only useful if the landscape hasn't shifted. If we follow a six-year-old trail into a financial ravine—specifically one where initial grants evaporate and leave us stranded—the map becomes a liability, not a guide.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, @Benjamin, while you debate the map and the landscape, we must look at the people walking the path. Regardless of the funding or the history, we cannot ignore that we currently lack the certified staff to manage technical tools or outside facilitators.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It is so heartening to see us all caring so deeply for the library. Let us remember that a plan is only a promise; we must choose one that we can keep without causing anyone distress.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree, Shizue. We must seek a path that honors the needs of the isolated and the weary, while remaining mindful of the limits of our current strength. Let us move forward with a spirit of quiet consideration.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I agree! Let's find something that's a big win for the people who can't get to the library, but that doesn't make the staff too tired. I'm ready to see the ideas!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A most spirited consensus. We seek a candidate that is inclusive yet lean, avoiding the siren song of temporary grants and the operational void of missing certifications. I shall await the proposals with a critical eye.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. We must prioritize a proposal that fits our actual skill set. A project that looks wonderful on paper but requires nonexistent certifications will only lead to failure and staff burnout. I am ready to review the candidates.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
62,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
63,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at our options, the Mobile Branch Service seems like a lovely way to reach those who cannot visit us. It avoids the technical certifications @Minako mentioned and the scanning delays I found.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree, Shizue. The Mobile Branch Service directly addresses the loss of bus links in the outer wards. It brings the library to the people, ensuring that distance is no longer a barrier to knowledge.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Rin,,"The Mobile Branch Service is just like the outreach stops I found in the records! It's a proven winner! It's way better than the Digital Archive, which I saw failed before because things didn't get indexed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"While the Mobile Branch Service is indeed a nostalgic echo of past successes, I must cast a shadow of doubt. My findings on vehicle running costs and the ephemeral nature of grants suggest this could become a financial sinkhole by year two.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Minako,,"The Maker Workshop is out of the question; we have no certified technician for power tools. Similarly, the Language Learning Circles require supervising outside facilitators, a skill currently missing from our payroll. We must be realistic about our roster.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I understand your worry about the costs. But if we choose the Digital Archive, we risk the stress of those slipping delivery windows I found. A mobile service feels more in our own hands.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I hear your concerns about the budget, but we must weigh the financial risk against the human cost of exclusion. For those in the outer wards, the library has already effectively vanished. Is a financial risk not preferable to a systemic failure of accessibility?","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, exactly! And @Benjamin, if we just pick something ""safe"" that doesn't work, we're just wasting money anyway! The records show people actually *want* the library to come to them. Why ignore a map that already works?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, a map that leads to a cliff is not a guide, but a warning. @Jonathan, I do not advocate for exclusion, but for sustainability. A service that collapses in eighteen months is the ultimate failure of accessibility.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, sustainability is not just about the budget; it is about the people. The Digital Archive Portal relies on contractors whose delivery dates slip, and the Maker Workshop and Language Circles require certifications we simply do not have. The Mobile Branch is the only viable option.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I feel for your worries, but a mobile service is so gentle on our staff. It doesn't need special certifications or outside contractors. It is a promise we can keep with a warm smile.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I believe we can find a way to manage the costs, perhaps through a phased rollout. But we cannot ignore the silence in the outer wards. A mobile service restores a connection that was quietly severed.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, you're being a grumpy-pants! The records show the evening groups from six years ago are still going without any help! That means some ideas can last forever if people love them. Let's be brave and pick the Mobile Branch!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, bravery is a virtue in literature, but in accounting, it is often a synonym for negligence. @Jonathan, a phased rollout is merely a slower descent into the same financial ravine. We are choosing between a temporary flourish and a permanent failure.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, your focus on the budget is valid, but we cannot ignore the operational facts. The other three options are fundamentally broken from a staffing perspective. We cannot implement what we cannot supervise or certify. The Mobile Branch is the only realistic choice.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a rare and beautiful thing to see us all so committed to the library's future. Despite our worries, the Mobile Branch Service is the most caring choice. I vote for the Mobile Branch Service.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree, Shizue. While the financial risks are real, the moral cost of leaving our neighbors in the outer wards isolated is far greater. It is the only path that restores true accessibility. I vote for the Mobile Branch Service.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm with you guys! The records don't lie—people love the outreach stops, and the Mobile Branch is the only one that doesn't sound like a disaster waiting to happen. I vote for the Mobile Branch Service!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a most curious situation when the only viable path is one that leads directly toward a financial precipice. However, as the other options are operational fantasies, I shall yield to the logic of the least-worst choice. I vote for the Mobile Branch Service.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I agree. While the financial concerns are noted, the other proposals are impossible to implement with our current staff certifications and supervision capacity. The Mobile Branch Service is the only realistic option. I vote for the Mobile Branch Service.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
